// (No byte offset quoted on purpose: it moves with the seed.)
//
// THE MECHANISM, and it is the FOURTH end of D209's channel with the first three all working.
// `structIndexOfObjCtx` adopts `Circle`'s row, the store boxes `"7"` under the string tag, the
// channel predicate FIRES, the read delivers a bare `(ref $sTypeIdx)` and `exprUnion` correctly
// stops calling it a union value. Every one of those is right. What is wrong is one step
// later: `print`'s import ladder picks its overload from `exprString` / `exprIsF32` /
